      "id": 13077,
      "name": "jasonshif",
      "username": "jasonshif",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jasonshif/{size}/2278_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-30T14:22:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My friend and I recently decided to play a silly little game with sentinels.&nbsp; We wanted to play a team of almost entirely heroes that require a lot of setup.&nbsp; This game lasted four and a half hours.</p><p>To start our endeavor, we picked Unity, Captain Cosmic, Scholar and Argent Adept in that order.&nbsp; We picked to fight La Capitan in Freedom Tower.&nbsp; On our first turn, almost nothing had been done.&nbsp; La Capitan had her turn and then it was our chance to shine.&nbsp; Except, we were more like a dull bulb.&nbsp; Captain Cosmic was able to get two constructs out(using his power for the second), however they were both defensive constructs.&nbsp; On Unity's turn she had absolutely no Golems in her hand and nothing to search her deck for them, so her turn was skipped to draw two cards: Modular Workbench and Volatile Parts.&nbsp; Then came scholar's turn.&nbsp; Scholar was able to play Flesh to Iron and then ended his turn(Having taken no damage).&nbsp; Argent played one instrument and ended his turn.</p><p>La Capitan played one crew and dealt damage to the lowest HP hero Target,&nbsp; goodbye construct.&nbsp; Cosmic's turn: play two more defensive constructs.&nbsp; This was a really bad hand.&nbsp; Unity's turn, still no golems.&nbsp; Even her draw was unlucky, she drew a scrapmetal and robot reclamation.&nbsp; Scholar's turn was just about as uneventful, drawing two cards.&nbsp; We didn't want to set up Scholar until he had cards to discard for his forms.&nbsp; Argent played a single melody and ended his turn(Nobody needed healing).&nbsp;</p><p>This was basically the entire game for three hours, Cosmic played more constructs, they died on the villain turn.&nbsp; Freedom tower gave us all the rooms and the entrypoints went over the rooms that hurt us the most.&nbsp; We barely got hurt, but La Capitan remained at full health the entire time.&nbsp; We almost gave up four times(and we probably should have).&nbsp;</p><p>After the third hour, we finally started picking up, Unity started getting bots out and they lasted for more than a turn thanks to redirecting damage.&nbsp; Scholar had started pumping out forms like there was no tomorrow and we could finally deal damage.&nbsp; After which, we did a steady 20 damage per turn to at least one target(Unity had almost every bot on the field, missing one raptorbot that La Capitan stole).&nbsp; From there we pretty much decimated her, even if it took some time(Thanks to her crew being in the way).&nbsp; We decided afterwards that we didn't want to play against La Capitan for a very long time.</p>",
